# Copy to .env and adjust. Never commit .env.
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=5000
# Local MongoDB from `npm run db:up`. On Heroku, set MONGODB_URI to the Atlas connection string.
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/hanyu
# Translation grading (the web app's only LLM calls; grading is off without it), and the offline
# passage and grader-eval scripts. On Heroku, set it as a config var; it never reaches the client.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Grading limits: per user in any 24 hours, and across all users per calendar month (UTC).
# GRADING_DAILY_LIMIT=20
# GRADING_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=10
# Daily reminders (web push); they're off without all three. Generate the keys once with
# `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`: changing them cuts off every subscribed device. The subject is
# a mailto: or https: URL that push services can contact you at. On Heroku, set them as config vars.
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=
# Recorded audio (npm run audio:generate, offline only; Heroku never needs these). From the Azure
# portal: your Speech resource's Keys and Endpoint page. The region is its location, e.g. eastus.
# AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
# AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=
# Optional: run the database integration tests (server/test/seed.test.ts) against this server.
# MONGODB_TEST_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017
